BC-250 CH7218/Q80A fix: cap output bpc to the sink's FRL budget on
DP->HDMI PCON links.

The CH7218 decodes the DSC-compressed DP stream and re-encodes it as
uncompressed FRL towards the TV. DC validation only checks the DP link
budget (compressed stream fits HBR2 easily), so a 4K120 RGB mode at
16 bpc - the driver's default max_bpc when nobody clamps it, e.g. a
cold boot straight into gamescope - passes validation and then loses
the picture, because 4K120 RGB 16bpc needs ~57 Gbps uncompressed and
the sink tops out at FRL5 (40 Gbps). 10 bpc (~35.6 Gbps) fits, which
is exactly why KDE->gamescope worked: kwin persists max_bpc=10 on the
connector and gamescope inherits it.

Clamp requested_bpc in create_validate_stream_for_sink() for
DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER links to the highest even bpc that
fits display_info.hdmi.max_frl_rate_per_lane * max_lanes (raw FRL
rate; the empirical failure boundary sits between 10 and 12 bpc, so
the encoding overhead is intentionally not deducted). Gated by
dc->config.bc250_hdmi21 like the rest of the DSC/PCON family, so the
stock behavior is untouched when the feature is off.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index 0ebb2bea0..aa2f73ca2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -8693,6 +8695,27 @@ create_validate_stream_for_sink(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	     aconnector->dc_link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type == DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER))
 		bpc_limit = 8;
 
+	/*
+	 * BC-250 CH7218 fix: DP->HDMI PCONs decode the DSC stream and
+	 * re-encode it as uncompressed FRL towards the sink. DC validation
+	 * only checks the DP link budget, so deep-color modes that exceed
+	 * the sink's FRL capacity (e.g. 4K120 RGB at 12+ bpc on a 40 Gbps
+	 * FRL5 sink) pass validation and then lose the picture. Cap the
+	 * requested bpc to what fits the sink's advertised FRL budget.
+	 */
+	if (aconnector && adev->dm.dc->config.bc250_hdmi21 &&
+	    aconnector->dc_link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type == DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER &&
+	    connector->display_info.hdmi.max_frl_rate_per_lane &&
+	    connector->display_info.hdmi.max_lanes) {
+		u64 frl_bps = (u64)connector->display_info.hdmi.max_frl_rate_per_lane *
+			      connector->display_info.hdmi.max_lanes * 1000000000ULL;
+		int frl_bpc = (int)(frl_bps / ((u64)drm_mode->clock * 3000));
+
+		frl_bpc = clamp(frl_bpc, 8, 16) & ~1;
+		if (requested_bpc > frl_bpc)
+			requested_bpc = frl_bpc;
+	}
+
 	do {
 		drm_dbg_kms(connector->dev, "Trying with %d bpc\n", requested_bpc);
 		stream = create_stream_for_sink(connector, drm_mode,
